// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/reproduce/contracts.t27 -- the t27 contracts gHashTag/trinity consumes, locked byte for byte
; S12 of gHashTag/trinity#988 (gHashTag/trinity#989): consume the canonical t27 manifest and
; specifications byte-identically, with a pinned revision and compiler hashes. The project manifest of
; S01 (gHashTag/t27 specs/trinity/project.t27) says the consumer vendors a byte-identical copy and
; generates its manifest from these files; nothing in this repository is a second authored registry.
; The copies are external/t27/<the same path as in t27>. The set is not chosen here: every file of
; t27's specs/trinity/, every t27 path a capability card names as CANONICAL_SPEC, IMPLEMENTATION or
; GENERATED (a directory whole), and tools/trinity_manifest.py, the checker those cards answer to.
; tools/contracts.py vendor is the only writer of external/t27 and of the data below; check holds the
; copies to it, check --upstream holds it to t27 at the revision, and check --t27c runs the pinned
; compiler over every vendored .t27. The website mirror (apps/website/public/t27/files) is a catalog
; snapshot and not this: a tarball of t27 master with files of a second branch laid over it, no hash
; per file, and a compiler wasm of unrecorded origin.
; The compiler is t27c, the package bootstrap/ of t27's Cargo workspace, built from the workspace root
; (cargo build --release --locked -p t27c); COMPILER_IDS are the git object ids, at the revision, of
; what that build reads: the root manifest and lock, and the package's manifest, build script and sources. Not a claim that the vendored contracts are true of this repository:
; holding the code to them is the capability index, the next part of S12.
; ASCII only (L3). phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module reproduce_contracts;

